  "body": "Stacked on #563 (branch `issue/220-trochoidal-slot`); merges after it.\n\nFollow-ups from the high-tier review of #563: each of the three is now a named refusal, never a misleading message or a silent substitute (Prime Directive).\n\n## What changed\n\n1. **Loop-cap refusal names its cause** (`trochoid_slot.rs`). When every rung of the step ladder needs more than the 20000-loop cap, the refusal now reads \"the forward step is too small - a 0.0001 mm forward step along the 40.000 mm centre line needs more than the 20000 loop cap ...; raise the forward step\". Before, it said \"the least, inf deg at (0.000, 0.000), was read at a 0.0001 mm step\". When longer rungs were measured over the engagement limit and the shorter ones hit the cap, the engagement refusal stays and adds the cap as the reason no shorter step was tried.\n2. **Microlift height bound: the clearance above the cut top.**\n   - App: `OpParams::microlift_refusal(clearance, top)` in `operation/types/sane.rs` holds the rule. `operation::microlift_sane` asks it with resolved heights, and `heights_gate` (create, parameter edit, source change) calls that and refuses by name.\n   - Motion: `TrochoidParams::validate` refuses the same law as a backstop, so no feed return is posted above the clearance plane.\n   - Why the clearance plane and not a stated maximum: see `docs/decisions/774-trochoid-refusals.md`.\n3. **Helix-turn cap is a refusal.** `helix_turns(..).unwrap_or(1.0)` is gone. A level whose bore needs more than `MAX_HELIX_TURNS` (1024) turns is refused by name, giving the drop, the helix radius and the fix (a smaller stepdown or a wider loop band). `emit_level` now returns `Result`.\n4. Refactor for the 400-line limit: `contained` and `arc_samples` move unchanged from `trochoid_slot.rs` (now 397 lines) to `trochoid_loops.rs` (336 lines).\n\n## How tested\n\nNew pinning tests. Each one fails on the #563 head without this change:\n- `crates/motion/tests/trochoid_slot.rs`\n  - `trochoid_step_past_the_loop_cap_is_refused_by_that_cause`: before, the refusal read \"... the least, inf deg at (0.000, 0.000) ...\".\n  - `trochoid_microlift_above_the_clearance_plane_is_refused`: before, a 100 mm lift returned `Ok`. A lift exactly at the bound is still accepted.\n  - `trochoid_bore_past_the_helix_turn_cap_is_refused`: before, a 6200 mm single level returned `Ok`, cutting the whole drop in one helix turn.\n- `crates/app/tests/trochoid_op.rs`\n  - `a_microlift_above_the_clearance_plane_is_refused_at_the_door`: before, `CreateOperation` accepted a 100 mm lift. The test also covers a refused edit that leaves the op unchanged, and an edit at the bound that is accepted.\n\nAlso run, all green:\n- full `trochoid_slot` (motion, 10 tests) and `trochoid_op` (app, 5 tests)\n- the motion lib trochoid unit tests\n- app lib `operation::` (71 tests)\n- `fanuc_post` (11 tests)\n- `golden_cl` `trochoid_slot_small_matches_golden`: the golden is unchanged, because a normal slot never reaches any of the three refusals\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n- Linux quick gate (`--base upstream/main`, so it also covers the #563 diff): green. Motion, app and ui suites passed, 0 failed, 12.8 min\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The partial case (some rungs measured over the limit, shorter rungs capped) is not pinned by its own test. Its message branch is the engagement refusal plus a suffix.\n- No GUI hand-check. The UI edits go through `EditOperationParams`, which now refuses with the named message.\n- No new command, so no MCP tool is needed.\n\nChangelog: Trochoidal slot refuses by name a forward step past the loop cap, a microlift above the clearance plane (at command creation) and a bore past the helix-turn cap, instead of a misleading message or a silent one-turn helix (#774)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated).\n\nfork synced at v0.16.0\n\nFixes #774\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
